    "result_text": "Done. The build compiles cleanly across all three repository profiles and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe new `customerCode` format is `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, with the sequence scoped per-city (one more than the owners already in that city). I kept each piece of logic in its natural home rather than bolting it onto one class:\n\n- **`CustomerCodeGenerator`** \u2014 new signature `generate(city, lastName, cityOwnerCount)` producing `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`. Factored the \"upper-cased first three letters\" rule into a private `prefix(...)` helper so it isn't duplicated for city and last name.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 now passes the owner's city and a per-city count instead of the global owner count.\n- **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `countOwnersByCity(String city)`, delegating to the repository (mirroring the existing `countOwners`).\n- **`OwnerRepository`** + all three profile implementations (`SpringDataOwnerRepository`, `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) \u2014 added `countByCity(String city)`, using a case-insensitive match consistent with the existing `findByLastNameIgnoreCase` queries.\n\n## Values derived from `customerCode`\n\nThe membership number in `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipNumber` builds `\"%s-M%02d\"` directly from `getCustomerCode()`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0001-M26`) with no change needed. That's the only derived value in the codebase \u2014 I grepped `getCustomerCode`/`customerCode` to confirm.\n\nThe acceptance test asserting `customerCode` matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` passes.",
